                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1153 Texas Co./3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-14T15:00:00-04:00">June 14, 1930—3
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>197. The Texas Company has reported that military authorities in Honan under
                    threat of confiscation of company’s goods stored in rented warehouse at Taokow
                    have extorted silver dollars twenty-five thousand in illegal taxes. Please radio
                    briefly circumstances and the steps taken or contemplated by the company,
                    Consulate General and Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
